# Line-ending policy.
#
# This is not a style preference. `choir_prototype/freeze.py` pins non-Python
# files by content hash, so a CRLF conversion on checkout changes those hashes
# and makes `python -m choir_prototype --frozen` report the frozen architecture
# as MODIFIED on a machine that has changed nothing.
#
# Without this file, a fresh clone on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, the default)
# fails the project's own freeze verification. Python modules survive, because
# they are pinned by normalised syntax tree rather than by bytes; Markdown does
# not. Normalising to LF everywhere keeps the archival record verifiable off
# the machine that produced it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.exe binary
*.node binary
